---
import Journey from '../../layouts/Journey.astro';
import Step from '../../components/journey/Step.astro';
import Next from '../../components/journey/Next.astro';
import More from '../../components/journey/More.astro';
import CopyPrompt from '../../components/site/CopyPrompt.astro';
import { url } from '../../lib/nav';
---
<Journey chapter="fleet" first="twenty" title="Twenty in a loop" description="A lead, a queue of tasks, up to twenty builders and a check in front of the main branch. You read what gets through the check.">
  <Step id="twenty" title="Twenty agents, one loop">
    <p>Everything so far in one loop: <a href={url('journey/lead/')}>the lead</a>, <a href={url('journey/parallel/')}>a copy each</a>, <a href={url('journey/check/')}>the check</a> before main. Each builder fills its own window, sends its result to the check and starts the next task with an empty one.</p>
    <div class="controls">
      <label class="control"><span>Builders <output>20</output></span>
        <input type="range" min="1" max="20" step="1" value="20" data-bind="n" />
      </label>
    </div>
    <More title="A brief for the lead">
      <CopyPrompt compact title="Start a lead">{`You are the lead. Do not build anything yourself.
Split the work in tasks.md into tasks one builder can finish alone. Start each builder in its own worktree with a brief: the goal, the files, what not to touch, how to check it.
When a builder reports, run the tests on its branch. Merge what passes, one branch at a time. Send the rest back.
Keep one line per task in status.md. Stop and ask me when two tasks need the same file or the decision is mine.`}</CopyPrompt>
    </More>
  </Step>
  <Step id="nogate" title="Take the check away">
    <p>In this made-up fleet one task in four comes back wrong. Without the check, those land on main.</p>
    <div class="pick">
      <button type="button" data-do="gate" data-val="off" data-default aria-pressed="true">No check</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="gate" data-val="on" aria-pressed="false">With the check</button>
    </div>
  </Step>
  <Step id="yours" title="What is left for you">
    <p>Deciding what gets built, and reading what the check lets through. The twenty windows are not yours to read.</p>
    <Next from="fleet" more={[{ href: 'models/', text: 'Which model where' }, { href: 'journey/meter/#many', text: 'What a fleet costs' }]} />
  </Step>
</Journey>
